  "line": "Bethel, once called Luz, was a city in Canaan where Jacob met God in a dream and named the place \"house of God.\"",
  "moments": [
    {
      "title": "Jacob's dream",
      "text": "On his way to Haran, Jacob dreamed of a ladder reaching to heaven, and the LORD promised him land and descendants. Jacob named the place Bethel, which had been called Luz.",
      "passage": "Genesis 28:10-19"
    },
    {
      "title": "Jacob returns to Bethel",
      "text": "God told Jacob to go up to Bethel and build an altar. Jacob had his household put away foreign gods, then built the altar there and called the place El-bethel.",
      "passage": "Genesis 35:1-7"
    },
    {
      "title": "Israel weeps and asks God",
      "text": "In the war against Benjamin, the Israelites went up to Bethel to ask God who should fight first. After a hard defeat, they wept, fasted, and offered sacrifices there, and the LORD told them to fight.",
      "passage": "Judges 20:18-28"
    },
    {
      "title": "Jeroboam's golden calf",
      "text": "King Jeroboam made two golden calves and set one up in Bethel. He also ordained a feast, made offerings on an altar there, and appointed priests for the high places.",
      "passage": "1 Kings 12:28-33"
    },
    {
      "title": "A man of God speaks against the altar",
      "text": "A man of God from Judah came to Bethel by the LORD's word and cried out against Jeroboam's altar. When the king stretched out his hand and ordered, \"Seize him!\", his hand withered, and the altar split apart.",
      "passage": "1 Kings 13:1-5"
    }
  ],
